2026-10-09T02:14:10.1126650Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1227175Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1237785Z [0m
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1239194Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1239984Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1240201Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1240736Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1241336Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1241609Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1241867Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1242421Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1242601Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1243083Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1243609Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1244042Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1244386Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1244536Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1244758Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1245003Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1245253Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1245619Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1245740Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1245859Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1246013Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1249762Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1250657Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1257311Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1257870Z I will:
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1258078Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1258434Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1259154Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1259911Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1260581Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1261029Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1261523Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1262233Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1262612Z    /root
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1274319Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1275002Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1292142Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1293106Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1293550Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1293941Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1294570Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1307686Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1308739Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1319342Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1320086Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1320860Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1321198Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1321503Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1321900Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1322364Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1323429Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1323929Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1324188Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1324489Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1324662Z 
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1325140Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T02:14:10.1325763Z   $ sh ./install-nix
